    ts:eventAt "2026-11-21T08:03:09+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    ts:memberOfOrigin <https://example.org/trendscout/origin/6392808b6d8e4eb2> ;
    ts:observedAt "2026-11-21T08:03:09+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    ts:originClusterId "6392808b6d8e4eb2" ;
    ts:passage "At Composio, we are building infrastructure that allows agents to communicate with the tools you use for work including Github, Gmail, Notion, Salesforce, etc. We are a small team of engineers wrangling problems from context to search, that help us provide the most capable bridge between your agents and your tools. We raised a $25M Series A from Lightspeed https://lsvp.com/stories/investing-in-composio-building-the-backbone-of-ai-agent-intelligence/ with some incredible angels like Guillermo Rauch (CEO of Vercel), Dharmesh Shah (CTO of Hubspot), Gokul Rajaram. Beginning of this year we 3x our ARR, our customers range from your friends in the YC batch to Wabi, Glean, Zoom and many more. WHAT YOU'LL DO? - own sourcing across every open role - Github, X, hackathon leaderboards, paper authors, open source communities, and the places our customers live - run technical screens yourself: read code, ask useful follow-ups, and separate signal from noise - build the recruiting playbook we do not have yet - outreach, rubrics, calibration, scorecards, and weekly hiring reviews - own pipeline metrics and tell us where the system is broken: conversion, source quality, time to offer, and offer acceptance - partner with engineering and GTM leads to turn vague hiring needs into target profiles, sourcing plans, and screens we trust - dogfood Composio to automate outreach, candidate tracking, and reporting \"MUST HAVES\" if you are very good, nothing is a must per-se - technical recruiting - you can read code well enough to evaluate a take-home or Github profile without an engineer in the room - you have built a recruiting process from scratch, not just inherited one - operator - you can bring structure to ambiguous hiring needs and keep the loop moving without founder babysitting - ai native - you use LLMs in your daily workflow - you are comfortable writing small scripts or agents to automate repetitive work - typist - you can write clear outreach, rubrics, docs, and hiring notes - human - you build trust and admit what you do not know OPTIONAL - founding recruiter or agency experience at a developer tools or infra company - experience hiring across both engineering and GTM - presence in developer communities through events, Discord, X, or open source" ;
