    ts:eventAt "2026-11-21T08:03:09+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    ts:memberOfOrigin <https://example.org/trendscout/origin/6392808b6d8e4eb2> ;
    ts:observedAt "2026-11-21T08:03:09+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    ts:originClusterId "6392808b6d8e4eb2" ;
    ts:passage "At Composio, we are building infrastructure that allows agents to communicate with the tools you use for work including Github, Gmail, Notion, Salesforce, etc. We are a small team of engineers wrangling problems from context to search, that help us provide the most capable bridge between your agents and your tools. We raised a $25M Series A from Lightspeed https://lsvp.com/stories/investing-in-composio-building-the-backbone-of-ai-agent-intelligence/ with some incredible angels like Guillermo Rauch (CEO of Vercel), Dharmesh Shah (CTO of Hubspot), Gokul Rajaram. Beginning of this year we 3x our ARR, our customers range from your friends in the YC batch to Wabi, Glean, Zoom and many more. WHAT YOU'LL DO? - own scheduling for every open role - phone screens, technical loops, and onsites across SF and Bangalore - so no candidate waits on us - run onsites end-to-end: travel, agendas, interviewer prep, lunch, and the person who greets the candidate at the door - keep Ashby clean: stages current, scorecards chased, feedback in within 24 hours, and no candidate left without a next step - be the candidate's point of contact from first call to offer, with fast replies and crisp updates - coordinate offers, reference checks, and the handoff to onboarding - surface where the loop is slow: time in stage, interviewer load, reschedules, and drop-off - dogfood Composio to automate scheduling, reminders, candidate tracking, and reporting \"MUST HAVES\" if you are very good, nothing is a must per-se - recruiting coordination - you have run high-volume scheduling across time zones without dropping threads - you have worked in an ATS and left it cleaner than you found it - operator - you can keep 30+ open roles moving without founder babysitting - ai native - you use LLMs in your daily workflow - you have bias towards working from a chat interface/cli rather than the UI - typist - you can write clear candidate emails, interview briefs, and hiring notes - human - you build trust and admit what you do not know OPTIONAL - recruiting coordinator or people ops experience at a fast-growing startup - experience coordinating both engineering and GTM hiring - event or travel planning experience" ;
