    ts:contentHash "b7435ef2a20303c84b4d38bc5276478f531e81d5fed9ad46abe37eff711c4175" ;
    ts:documents <https://example.org/trendscout/job-posting/ashby/pinecone/7e7c824d-17a6-44ea-9485-6f04ceea5f29> ;
    ts:eventAt "2026-11-21T08:03:11+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    ts:memberOfOrigin <https://example.org/trendscout/origin/5500bae7aa0aa192> ;
    ts:observedAt "2026-11-21T08:03:11+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    ts:originClusterId "5500bae7aa0aa192" ;
    ts:passage "ABOUT PINECONE Pinecone is the trusted AI knowledge company. Its trusted AI knowledge platform - including its Database, Nexus, and Marketplace products - power accurate, fast, and cost-effective AI applications for more than 10,000 customers and 1M developers worldwide. Pinecone's mission is to make AI knowledgeable. For more information, visit pinecone.io http://pinecone.io. ABOUT THE ROLE/TEAM: As an Enterprise PMM, you will help enterprise technical decision makers and AI leaders, including CTOs, enterprise architects, and Chief AI Officers, understand why Pinecone is the platform to standardize on for knowledgeable AI. You will accomplish this through platform messaging and positioning, solutions marketing, executive-level content, and deep partnership with our enterprise sales team. You will work closely with Product, Sales, Solutions Engineering, Customer Success, Partners, and Marketing to present Database, Nexus, and Marketplace as one platform that solves the knowledge problems for enterprise AI. RESPONSIBILITIES: - Platform and Solutions Marketing: - Own the Pinecone platform narrative: how Database, Nexus, and Marketplace work together, and why enterprises should standardize on Pinecone over point tools, hyperscaler, and DIY alternatives. - Package the platform into solutions for the AI initiatives enterprises are funding, such as AI platforms, enterprise search, recommendation systems, and AI agents, with reference architectures and business cases built alongside Solutions Engineering. - Partner with customers on enterprise case studies and run win/loss analysis, feeding what you learn back into messaging and the roadmap. - Enterprise GTM: - Speak credibly to technical decision makers and Chief AI Officers in executive briefings, customer advisory boards, analyst sessions, and strategic deal reviews. - Equip enterprise AEs and SEs to sell the platform with pitch decks, discovery guides, talk tracks, battlecards, and TCO and ROI models, and join strategic deals to sharpen positioning. - Lead launches for platform and enterprise capabilities, and supply the narrative for enterprise campaigns, ABM programs, events, and cloud and SI co-marketing. REQUIREMENTS: - 7+ years of experience in product marketing, solutions marketing, or technical GTM, ideally at an AI/ML infrastructure, data, or cloud platform company selling to the enterprise. - Proven track record building a platform narrative for a multi-product portfolio and getting a field organization to adopt it. - Strong technical acumen: you can whiteboard an AI application architecture (embeddings, retrieval, LLMs, agents, data pipelines) and hold your own with an enterprise architect. - Executive presence with experience presenting to and influencing C-level and VP-level buyers, including CTOs, CIOs, or Chief AI Officers. - Deep partnership with enterprise sales: you've built enablement reps actually use and helped navigate large, multi-stakeholder deals. - Ability to build business value cases (TCO, ROI, risk reduction) that survive procurement and finance review. - AI-native workflow from content creation to automating away process - Experience working cross-functionally with Product, Engineering, Developer Relations, and Sales teams. - Excellent written and verbal communication skills. BONUS POINTS: - Prior experience as a solutions engineer, solutions architect, or developer. - Familiarity with vector databases, retrieval-augmented generation (RAG), or search technologies. - Experience with enterprise requirements such as security reviews, compliance, data residency, and BYOC or private deployments. PERKS & BENEFITS: - Comprehensive health coverage including medical, dental, vision, and mental health resources - 401(k) Plan - Equity award - Flexible time off - Paid parental leave - Annual Company Retreat - WFH Equipment Stipend All qualified applicants will receive considerations for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, disability, marital status, familial status, sexual orientation, pregnancy, gender identity, gender expression, national origin, ancestry, citizenship status, veteran status, and any other legally protected status under federal, state, or local anti-discrimination laws." ;
